    "content": "Denver, Colorado, is nicknamed the \"Mile High City\" because its official elevation is exactly one mile (5,280 feet or 1,609 meters) above sea level. Located at the edge of the Rocky Mountains, it is a major hub for outdoor activities, culture, and business, known for its high-altitude, dry climate and sunny days. Key Aspects of Denver (The Mile High City): Elevation Marker: The 13th step of the Colorado State Capitol building and a row of seats in Coors Field are famously located exactly 5,280 feet above sea level. Location & Geography: Situated in north-central Colorado, it serves as a gateway to the Rocky Mountains. Activities: The city is popular for its proximity to skiing, hiking, biking, and rafting, alongside attractions like the Red Rocks Amphitheatre. Climate: Due to the altitude, Denver is known for having thin air and a sunny, dry climate. Culture & Growth: It has grown from a19th-century mining town into a major metropolitan area with a thriving brewery scene, arts districts, and diverse food options. Important Information for Visitors: Altitude Adjustment: Visitors may feel the effects of lower oxygen levels, such as quicker fatigue. Best Time to Visit: The period from May to October offers the best weather for outdoor activities.",
